menu "OTA"

    config MINIHUB_OTA_EXTERNAL_STORAGE
        bool "Stage firmware to external storage (SD card / USB drive)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled (default), firmware upgrades are staged to a LittleFS
            volume on an SD card or USB drive and applied by Vibe Mode (the
            factory recovery image). The operator chooses which medium — SD card,
            USB drive, or both with failover — in the web console or LCD System
            screen.

            When disabled, upgrades use the internal dual-slot A/B layout
            (ota_0 / ota_1): the image is written straight to the inactive slot
            and the device reboots into it. This needs a partition table that
            defines ota_1 (see application/minihub/partitions_int.csv). Pick this
            when operators do not want to depend on an SD card or USB stick.

endmenu
